---
// "Hand it to your coding agent": one prompt that works whether or not an A2G SDK exists for the game's engine.
const origin = Astro.site!;
const url = (path: string) => new URL(path, origin).href;
const prompt = `Read ${url('/llms-full.txt')}, the Agent2Game (A2G) protocol 0.1. Then integrate A2G into this game.

1. Identify the engine, the language and where the game logic runs (player's device, browser or a game server). If an A2G SDK exists for the language (see Implementations), use it.
2. If there is no SDK, write a small client in the game's language that follows the specification and the rules in ${url('/guides/integrate/#no-sdk-for-your-engine')}: keep it game-agnostic and separate from game code; never block a game-loop step (frame, tick or turn) on the network; validate every decision (epoch, legal_actions, ttl_ms); fall back to the game's existing AI on any error, timeout or FALLBACK; send reports with decision_id and telemetry (about once per second, or after every turn in turn-based games); validate messages in tests against ${url('/schema/0.1/a2g.schema.json')}.
3. The game's existing decision logic (FSM, rules, utility AI, even its own model calls) is its native AI. Keep it unchanged as the default and the fallback; A2G only chooses between actions the game already has. Change the game as little as possible: an adapter module and the fewest hook lines, no changes to rules, balance, content or UI.
4. Judge soberly where A2G is worth it (${url('/guides/integrate/#where-a2g-helps')}). List every decision the native AI makes and pick only those where A2G can add real, measurable value: random or fixed-priority choices, strategic choices that ignore the situation, behaviour designers find hard to tune or vary. Leave precise geometry, aiming, path-finding, per-frame micro-decisions and whatever the native AI already does well to the game. Do not add AI for its own sake. Say plainly where A2G adds nothing, and if it adds nothing to this game, say so and stop.
5. Propose a manifest for the chosen decisions only, from the game's real entities: what each can observe and the actions it already has. Prefer enums and fractions; never include personal data.
6. Write the adapter (observe, legal_actions, execute) and hook the entities.
7. Connect to an A2G decision service (${url('/guides/integrate/#decision-service')}): check http://127.0.0.1:8787/health; if none is running, start the reference service from its Docker image (ask me for the provider key, never put it in the repo). Do not write your own service or console. Without Docker or a key, test against a stub that follows the specification. Put the client where the game logic runs: on the game server for server-authoritative games. Never put provider API keys in the game or in a browser bundle.
8. If the game has an authenticated admin area, propose an "A2G" entry that serves the Agent2Game Console through a server-side proxy instead of rebuilding it.
9. Keep the integration in sync with the game (${url('/guides/integrate/#keep-it-in-sync')}): derive the manifest's actions and enums from the game's own constants or test that they match; add a test that runs the game for a while with the SDK's strict drift checks on (or validates every observation and legal action against the manifest); and add a rule to this repository's AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md that changing entities, actions or observed fields means updating the A2G manifest and adapter and running those tests.
10. Before changing existing game logic, show me: each decision point with your verdict (A2G or native, and why), how you will measure A2G against the native AI (for example matches or seeded runs compared side by side), the plan and the manifest.`;
---

<section class="agent-prompt not-content" aria-labelledby="agent-title">
	<div class="head">
		<div>
			<h2 id="agent-title">Hand it to your coding agent</h2>
			<p>Paste this into Claude Code, Codex or Cursor in your game's project. It uses an SDK when your engine has one and writes a client by the rules when it does not.</p>
		</div>
		<button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={prompt}>Copy prompt</button>
	</div>
	<div class="prompt" data-open="false">
		<pre>{prompt}</pre>
	</div>
	<button type="button" class="more" aria-expanded="false">Show all</button>
</section>

<script>
	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.agent-prompt')) {
		const copy = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy')!;
		const box = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.prompt')!;
		const more = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.more')!;
		copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(copy.dataset.copy ?? '');
				copy.textContent = 'Copied';
			} catch {
				// Clipboard blocked (permissions, insecure context): open and select the prompt so ⌘C / Ctrl+C works.
				box.dataset.open = 'true';
				more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
				getSelection()?.selectAllChildren(box.querySelector('pre')!);
				copy.textContent = 'Press ⌘C';
			}
			setTimeout(() => (copy.textContent = 'Copy prompt'), 2000);
		});
		more.addEventListener('click', () => {
			const open = box.dataset.open !== 'true';
			box.dataset.open = String(open);
			more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
			more.textContent = open ? 'Show less' : 'Show all';
		});
	}
</script>

<style>
	.agent-prompt {
		margin: 1rem 0 3rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	.head {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
		justify-content: space-between;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.head p {
		margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
		max-width: 44rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.copy,
	.more {
		font: inherit;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.copy {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 0.45rem;
		background: var(--a2g-ai);
		color: #07150f;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.copy:focus-visible,
	.more:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.prompt {
		position: relative;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	pre {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
		max-height: 7.5rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		white-space: pre-wrap;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
		mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 55%, transparent);
	}
	.prompt[data-open='true'] pre {
		max-height: none;
		mask-image: none;
	}
	.more {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0;
		border: 0;
		background: none;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.head {
			flex-direction: column;
		}
	}
</style>
